  "body": "After the refactoring this section will say\r\n\r\n> If previousId was given, let id be previousId; otherwise, let id be an implementation-defined integer that is greater than zero that will identify the timeout to be set by this call in global's map of active timers.\r\n\r\nwhich is equivalent to what it says today. However, it seems a little bad that you have to infer from IDL what the maximum is here. I suspect to some extent it will depend on https://github.com/whatwg/infra/issues/87. Using typed integers to indicate the range would make the most sense to me as that is what implementations do already.",
